{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Implementation complete in worktree ../bluebottle-enrich-lock (branch bluebottle-enrich-lock, rebased onto origin/main c6828ef348 — Gerrit 1701 merged mid-work, so the planned stack collapsed to a plain rebase and the doctor delta lands in this same change).\n\nWhat shipped:\n- src/rebar/_store/lock_owner.py (401 LOC): the decision table extracted verbatim into _stamp_is_stale(stamp, artifact_path, *, fcntl_held, unrecognised_via_ceiling). _mkdir_lock_is_stale is now a thin reader passing unrecognised_via_ceiling=False, so its behaviour is unchanged (its OSError branch still short-circuits to the ceiling, and a non-v2 stamp still reaches _legacy_stamp_is_stale). New sibling stamped_file_is_stale(path) reads the stamp from the FILE and passes fcntl_held=False, unrecognised_via_ceiling=True.\n- src/rebar/llm/enrich_drain.py (340 LOC): _acquire_advisory_lock writes _owner_stamp() into the file after the O_EXCL create (best-effort, like the mkdir leg), and on FileExistsError consults stamped_file_is_stale. A stale lock is logged at WARNING with holder + age and unlinked, then the create is retried EXACTLY ONCE (a bounded for-range(2); a second collision returns None). drain()'s skip log moved INFO -> WARNING and now names the holder via a new _describe_drain_lock_holder helper.\n- src/rebar/_commands/doctor_locks.py: _existence_report decodes the stamp (holder/pid_state/held_seconds) and reports a real staleness verdict from stamped_file_is_stale. A free lock is now not-stale rather than not-assessable; not-assessable survives only on the degraded row emitted when a probe raises. Schema description + pinned doctor help text updated, docs/cli-reference.md regenerated.\n\nTests: 8 new drain-lock tests (stamp on acquire + release, dead-holder reclaimed end-to-end through drain(), aged-out unstamped orphan reclaimed, fresh unstamped lock respected, live holder honoured with bytes unchanged + WARNING naming pid, foreign host respected then aged out, exactly-two os.open attempts) and 3 rewritten doctor drain-leg tests. The three existing lock-owner suites (41 tests) pass untouched — the regression guard on the extraction.\n\nLocal gates so far: all runnable scripts/check_*.py = 0, complexity baseline --check (active=59 new=0 increased=0 stale=0), all four generators re-run with no diff, make lint green, make typecheck green (519 files). Full CI pytest invocation running."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786598866338708001,"uuid":"2eec08ab-3efe-488d-a5f2-ee69fe618792"}